# Ratchet demo VM settings. On the VM: cp .env.vm.example .env, then edit .env.
# Never commit .env. Never put real keys in this example file.
# Full reference: docs/DEPLOY_NEBIUS_VM.md and docs/CONFIGURATION.md
#
# Keep comments on their own lines: this file is read by Docker Compose and by deploy/vm/*.sh.

# --- Web address --------------------------------------------------------------
# Your DNS name (an A record pointing at the VM's public IP), e.g. gateway.example.com.
# No DNS yet? Use <public-ip>.sslip.io, e.g. 203.0.113.7.sslip.io: it resolves to that IP,
# so Caddy can get a real certificate at once. cloud-init fills this in on first boot if it
# is still the placeholder below.
RATCHET_DOMAIN=ratchet.example.com

# --- Simulation host (a second gateway, mock mode, beside the live one) ------------
# on: Caddy serves the mock gateway at RATCHET_SIM_DOMAIN (default sim.<RATCHET_DOMAIN>), where anyone can
# run days, break a deploy and watch the rollback, for free. It needs DNS for that name: automatic with
# sslip.io; with your own domain, add an A record (or a wildcard) first, or Caddy retries the certificate.
# off: no simulation host (the container still runs, unreachable); then also add an empty RATCHET_SIM_URL=.
RATCHET_SIM=on
# RATCHET_SIM_DOMAIN=sim.ratchet.example.com
# The live pages' link to it. Leave the line out: https://<RATCHET_SIM_DOMAIN>. Empty: no link.
# RATCHET_SIM_URL=
# Optional: signs the simulation's BOMs. Never the same key as RATCHET_BOM_SIGNING_KEY.
RATCHET_SIM_BOM_SIGNING_KEY=

# --- Mode ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# mock: simulated models, no keys, no cost. Start here.
# live: real Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory and real web search (costs money).
RATCHET_MODE=mock

# Mock only: simulated days to run at startup, so the dashboard opens on a student that
# has already been trained instead of a cold start. 0 turns it off.
RATCHET_MOCK_WARMUP_DAYS=4

# SQLite ledger inside the ratchet-data volume (live mode; mock mode keeps it in memory).
RATCHET_DB=/data/ratchet.db

# --- Live mode keys (leave empty in mock mode) ---------------------------------
# Token Factory API key: teacher, judge and fallback student.
NEBIUS_API_KEY=
# Tavily Search key for Scout's searcher agent.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Student on a Nebius Serverless Endpoint (vLLM). Leave both empty to use the hosted,
# untuned fallback student on Token Factory (pay per token, no GPU running).
RATCHET_STUDENT_BASE=
RATCHET_STUDENT_KEY=

# --- Budget guard for the public demo (live mode) ------------------------------
# Most Scout may spend per UTC day, in USD. When reached, Scout answers 429.
# 0.50/day keeps the worst case over Oct 29 - Dec 15 (48 days) at $24, inside the $25 Builder credit.
RATCHET_SCOUT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=0.50
# Scout runs allowed per client IP per hour.
RATCHET_SCOUT_RUNS_PER_HOUR=6
# Scout runs allowed per UTC day across all visitors, judges included. Caps Tavily credits (about 3 searches
# per run). With the judges' reserve below, 22 leaves the public 15 runs a day.
RATCHET_SCOUT_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY=30
# Share of student answers also checked by the teacher. Each audit is a paid Ultra call.
RATCHET_AUDIT_RATE=0.05
# The counters above survive restarts and update.sh: they are kept in the ledger (live mode).

# --- Judges and Tavily credits (live mode; docs/CONFIGURATION.md) --------------
# Runs per UTC day held back for hackathon judges, unlocked by an access code that goes in the
# submission's testing instructions only (never on the project page, in the video or in a URL).
# Set both or neither. Generate the code with: openssl rand -hex 16
# RATCHET_SCOUT_JUDGE_CODE=
# RATCHET_SCOUT_JUDGE_RUNS_PER_DAY=7
# Judges' USD per day; unset = their share of the daily budget (7/22 of 0.50 = 0.15).
# RATCHET_SCOUT_JUDGE_BUDGET_USD=
# Tavily credits per cycle (free plan: 1,000 a month), the judges' share (unset = 7/22 of it),
# the day of the month the cycle starts (Tavily's reset day is unverified) and the date the
# daily allowance is spread until (the last day of judging).
# RATCHET_TAVILY_MONTHLY_CREDITS=1000
# RATCHET_TAVILY_JUDGE_CREDITS=
# RATCHET_TAVILY_CYCLE_DAY=1
# RATCHET_TAVILY_PACE_UNTIL=2026-12-15
# Threads that run those audits (and a shadow candidate's checks) after the answer is sent, so an
# audited request does not wait for the teacher. Empty = 4 in live mode, 0 in mock mode (every
# check before the answer, as the simulations expect). See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
RATCHET_SIDECAR_WORKERS=

# --- Edge access control (Caddy) ----------------------------------------------
# open:    Caddy lets every path through, including /v1/chat/completions; the app's keys decide.
# guarded: /v1/*, /openai/* (the Azure-style chat route) and /ratchet/demo/* need the header
#          X-Ratchet-Admin-Token: <token>.
#          The UI stays public at the edge: /, /scout, /dashboard, /ratchet/stats, /ratchet/bom
#          (the app's RATCHET_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD decides whether the last two need a key).
#          In mock mode this also disables the dashboard's Run day / Break / Reset buttons.
#          In live mode without RATCHET_API_KEYS, also set RATCHET_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED=1: the gateway then
#          starts only with RATCHET_API_GUARD=guarded and a RATCHET_ADMIN_TOKEN of 32+ characters.
RATCHET_API_GUARD=open
# At least 32 characters, hex only. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
RATCHET_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Gateway API keys (in the app, works with or without the Caddy guard) -------
# name:key pairs, comma-separated; each key at least 16 characters. When set, /v1/* and /openai/*
# need "Authorization: Bearer <key>" (what OpenAI SDKs send; also X-API-Key or api-key). Pages, Scout and /healthz stay public.
# Generate a key with: openssl rand -hex 24
RATCHET_API_KEYS=
# Requests per key per UTC day on /v1/chat/completions. 0 = unlimited.
RATCHET_API_KEY_DAILY_REQUESTS=0
# Seconds within which the same API client's repeat of a stored example counts once toward the
# frequent-request rule (an example seen 3 times leaves the golden set for training), so a client
# that retries without an Idempotency-Key cannot move golden examples. The app's default is 300 in
# live mode and 0 (every repeat counts) in mock mode; 300 here holds the public mock demo to the
# same rule. Without RATCHET_API_KEYS every visitor is one client.
RATCHET_SEEN_DEDUP_S=300
# Admin keys for task management (PUT/DELETE /ratchet/tasks/...), same syntax, never the same keys
# as RATCHET_API_KEYS. Empty: task writes are refused in live mode and open to anyone in mock mode.
# An admin key also reads the dashboard API.
RATCHET_ADMIN_KEYS=
# Read-only dashboard keys, same syntax, never an API or admin key. They read /ratchet/stats,
# /ratchet/cost, the task list and the BOMs when the dashboard is private, and write nothing.
RATCHET_DASHBOARD_KEYS=

# --- Spend and rate limits (docs/CONFIGURATION.md, Spend and rate limits) ---------
# What /v1/chat/completions may spend in a UTC day, all keys together, in US dollars at list
# prices (0 = no cap). block: every chat request gets a 429 past it; student_only: confident
# student answers go on and only requests that need the teacher get the 429. Scout has its own
# budget (RATCHET_SCOUT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD). budget events at 50, 80 and 100% go to the log.
RATCHET_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=0
RATCHET_BUDGET_MODE=block
# Every key's own caps (0 = none), and per-key overrides by name, e.g.
# RATCHET_KEY_LIMITS=me:daily_usd=2,rpm=30,concurrency=2
RATCHET_API_KEY_DAILY_USD=0
RATCHET_KEY_LIMITS=
# Requests a minute per client address when RATCHET_API_KEYS is empty (empty = 120 in live mode,
# 0 in mock mode). uvicorn takes the address from Caddy here.
RATCHET_IP_RPM=

# --- Who sees the dashboard and the docs (in the app) -----------------------------
# 1: the dashboard API (/ratchet/stats, /ratchet/cost, the task list, the BOMs) needs no key, so
# judges see the live dashboard. In live mode anonymous readers then get client pseudonyms
# (client-1, ...) and events without URLs or error messages; a request with an admin or dashboard
# key gets everything. 0 (the app's own default in live mode): it needs an admin or dashboard key,
# and the dashboard page, which sends no key yet, shows no data.
RATCHET_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD=1
# 1 keeps the BOM endpoints public for auditors when the dashboard is private. 0 = like the dashboard.
RATCHET_PUBLIC_BOM=0
# Live mode refuses to start without RATCHET_API_KEYS, because /v1/* would answer anyone on your
# Token Factory credits. Set 1 only when Caddy guards /v1/* instead: the gateway then also needs
# RATCHET_API_GUARD=guarded and a RATCHET_ADMIN_TOKEN of 32+ characters, or it refuses to start.
# Mock mode ignores it.
RATCHET_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED=0
# 1 once scripts/day1_check.py passed with a real key and the GPU rates in docs/CONFIGURATION.md match your Nebius bill.
# Until then every cost report labels its prices "unverified list prices". Ratchet never sets it for you.
RATCHET_PRICES_VERIFIED=0
# Optional Content-Security-Policy for every response. Empty = none. A value the pages work with
# is in docs/CONFIGURATION.md (Privacy and security); wrap it in double quotes here, because it
# holds single quotes and semicolons. /docs and /openapi.json exist in mock mode only, unless
# RATCHET_OPENAPI=1.
RATCHET_CSP=

# --- Logs and metrics (docs/CONFIGURATION.md, Observability) ---------------------
# Empty = text and WARNING in mock mode, json and INFO in live mode: one line per chat request
# (ids, route, cost, status; never prompt or answer text). `docker compose logs ratchet` shows them.
RATCHET_LOG_FORMAT=
RATCHET_LOG_LEVEL=
# Bearer token a Prometheus scraper sends to GET /metrics: at least 16 characters, not one of the
# keys above. Empty = only admin and dashboard keys read /metrics (anyone with RATCHET_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD=1).
RATCHET_METRICS_TOKEN=

# --- Privacy and provenance ------------------------------------------------------
# Replace emails, phone numbers, card numbers and similar with placeholders before storing
# training examples. 1 = on (default).
RATCHET_REDACT_PII=1
# Ed25519 key that signs each adapter's bill of materials. Generate on your laptop with
# `python -m ratchet.bom keygen` and publish the public key it prints. Empty = unsigned.
RATCHET_BOM_SIGNING_KEY=

# --- Optional: backups to Nebius Object Storage (deploy/vm/backup.sh) -----------
# s3://<bucket>/<prefix>. Empty = keep backups on the VM only.
RATCHET_BUCKET_S3=
# S3 endpoint for Object Storage. Copy it from the console (verify on day 1).
RATCHET_S3_ENDPOINT=

# --- Demo watchdog (python3 -m ratchet.watch; docs/DEPLOY_NEBIUS_VM.md#watchdog) --
# Where alerts go: an https:// webhook that takes {"text": ...} (Slack; Discord with /slack appended is UNVERIFIED).
# Run `python3 -m ratchet.watch test-alert` after setting it. Empty: alerts only reach /var/log/ratchet/watch.log.
# RATCHET_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# RATCHET_ALERT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# The probe's key: add `watchdog:<random key>` to RATCHET_API_KEYS, then set RATCHET_TASKS_FILE=/config/tasks.json
# (the pinned probe task, never stored) and, for a cap, RATCHET_KEY_LIMITS. Both must be set together: the file's
# `clients` names a key that must exist.
# RATCHET_TASKS_FILE=/config/tasks.json
# RATCHET_WATCH=on
# RATCHET_WATCH_CONNECT=public
# RATCHET_WATCH_HEARTBEAT_URL=
